          "brief": "Improve feeding practices in relevant locations to ensure sustainable intensification",
          "long_description": "To boost efficiency, producers should intensify production in extensive systems and promote livestock fattening solutions. They should also use more digestible feeds, provide seasonal feed supplementation - including, but not limited to, lipids - and adopt new feed solutions such as seaweed or insects. Crop residues could be used for feed, thereby improving their valuation and avoiding their burning. In parallel, planting pastures with improved grasses and legumes could enhance forage quality. Beyond increasing overall productivity, adapted feed can also help address specific challenges like methane emissions. For instance, seaweed or methane inhibitors added to existing feed recipes can reduce emissions from enteric fermentation.",
