          "brief": "Improve nutrient management through increased fertilizer application efficiency",
          "long_description": "Enhancing fertilizer application efficiency is key to improving nutrient management. This can be achieved by aligning application with soil and crop needs, reducing over-application in certain areas, shifting to smarter and more innovative fertilizers, and increasing the use of organic alternatives where possible. The cultivation of leguminous crops, as food, feed or cover crops, should be promoted since they support natural nitrogen fixation. Additionally, applying nitrogen inhibitors on crop fields can help limit N2O emissions.",
