          "number": "6L",
          "brief": "Protect land rights, especially for women",
          "long_description": "At both individual and community levels, securing land rights for vulnerable groups - especially women, youth, and Indigenous Peoples - is essential to addressing persistent inequalities in access and ownership. Strengthening these rights not only promotes social equity but also enables long-term investments in land stewardship. It is also important to develop the long-term valuation of soils as economic assets, including their carbon content, and to promote their use as potential collateral. This can help align economic and financial incentives with sustainable land management practices.",
