          "number": "5L",
          "brief": "Integrate restoration efforts into productive schemes through agroforestry, sylvopasture and paludiculture",
          "long_description": "68 percent of degraded land identified at the worldwide level as potentially biophysically available for restoration is considered as suited for mosaic restoration that consists in combining forests and trees with agriculture. In restored ecosystems, it is possible to combine carbon capture and preservation on the one hand and economic activities on the other through production of crops and livestock products. Alignment between restoration efforts with the development of forest value chains could be instrumental to channeling private finance and accelerating ecosystem restoration, and securing wood fibre needs to sustain the bioeconomy and generate employment and income in rural areas.",
