          "number": "7A",
          "brief": "Protect food through the use of improved technologies and enhanced storage facilities with limited GHG footprint",
          "long_description": "Reducing food loss and emissions, and protecting food, requires the deployment of improved technologies and enhanced storage facilities with a limited GHG footprint. For example, innovative cold storage solutions and low-scale storage options tailored for smallholders can be deployed. Investments should prioritize sustainable cooling systems powered by renewable energy to prevent spoilage without increasing emissions. Additionally, the optimal use of F-gases must be considered, as they contribute to global warming and constitute a rapidly growing source of GHG emissions due to increasing demand for cooling in response to climate-related volatility in agricultural primary production.",
