          "number": "7D",
          "brief": "Improve coordinated investments between private and public actors for increased investments in the food supply chain",
          "long_description": "Foster partnerships between public and private sectors to invest in infrastructure, logistics, and technology innovations that streamline the supply chain and minimize losses. Adjusting regulations and standards on food products could also reduce the amount of losses and waste. International trade cooperation or free trade agreements can help in moving perishable food products across borders faster, minimizing losses. Locally, joint efforts by the private sectors and food banks could help minimizing food waste and address social needs.",
