          "number": "7F",
          "brief": "Improve the targeting of food supply chain interventions to focus on high-loss areas (locations and commodities) through a nutrition and GHG lens",
          "long_description": "Interventions should be directed toward points in the food supply chain where losses or waste are highest, particularly when assessed through a nutrition and environmental lens. Priority should be given to specific value chains - such as fresh fruits and vegetables, or fish and meat. In high-income countries, targeting later stages of the supply chain can maximize GHG savings, while in low-income countries, early-stage interventions are more likely to actively support food security and nutrition outcomes.",
