              "long_description": "The National School Meals and Nutrition Strategy 2017–2022 calls for prioritising direct food purchases for the National School Meals and Nutrition Programme from local smallholder farmers, then regionally and nationally until supplies are adequate. Linking school meals to locally produced food is intended to support long-term food and nutrition security, schoolchildren, markets, smallholder farmers and other supply-chain actors.",
              "policy_document": "National School Meals and Nutrition Strategy 2017–2022",
