          "number": "9E",
          "brief": "Protect vulnerable groups, especially women, impacted by climate change through well-designed social safety net programs",
          "long_description": "Social safety net and public employment programs should explicitly incorporate climate vulnerability into their targeting criteria. They should also address the root causes of vulnerability to climate shocks and strengthen resilience through investments in human capital, adaptation efforts, and related activities. These programs should enable both anticipatory actions and ex-post responses. It is essential that women’s needs, challenges, and priorities are systematically integrated and adequately budgeted for in agrifood system and climate-related policies.",
