          "number": "9F",
          "brief": "Protect low-income and vulnerable groups from the side effects of mitigation or nutrition policies",
          "long_description": "Agrifood mitigation and nutrition policies may have unintended economic consequences for low-income and vulnerable groups, particularly when they lead to reduced production of certain commodities or shifts in prices and market incentives. These impacts should be addressed through well-designed compensation mechanisms. Adequate cash transfers and job training programs can help offset income losses and support transitions to alternative economic activities aligned with the evolving agrifood context.",
