          "number": "9H",
          "brief": "Improve social safety net programs to consider nutritional needs, especially for women, and promote healthy diets",
          "long_description": "In addition to income criteria, the specific nutritional needs of targeted populations should be considered to ensure that vulnerable groups are adequately supported by one scheme or another—such as cash transfers or food subsidies. Support should be notably provided to women since evidence shows that directing support to women is more likely to yield benefits for household diets and child health. In addition, food subsidies, whether in cash or in kind, should be structured to encourage the consumption of healthy diets.",
