          "brief": "Improve trade rules and global consultative processes to develop shared methods and recognitions for common environmental labels and certifications",
          "long_description": "Trade can play a key role in supporting mitigation efforts and reducing global agricultural GHG emissions - particularly when GHG externalities are included in pricing mechanisms, regulated through certification schemes, or communicated to consumers via labelling. To avoid market fragmentation and potential trade disputes, it is essential to reach consensus on how to define and calculate carbon footprints and to establish measures that facilitate trade in low-carbon footprint products.",
