          "number": "9N",
          "brief": "Improve science and policy interface",
          "long_description": "Support structured dialogue among scientists, policymakers, and other relevant stakeholders to promote inclusive science and evidence-based policymaking. This will enhance coherence, foster shared ownership, and enable collective action. Provide guidance on the importance of a regulatory environment that not only addresses risk management but also encourages innovation and the adoption of new technologies. Regulatory adjustments will be introduced to keep pace with the accelerating speed of innovation and evolving challenges, including those driven by climate change.",
